   "region:spinal-cord",
   "modality:sensory",
   "theory:lesion"
  ],
  "structures": [],
  "explain": "Visceral and somatic afferents converge on the same dorsal horn neurons, and the brain interprets the input as coming from the skin. Heart pain maps to T1-T4 dermatomes (left arm). The diaphragm is supplied by C3-C5 through the phrenic nerve, so its irritation is felt at the shoulder tip. The diaphragm is innervated by C3-C5 (phrenic nerve), the same dermatomes as the shoulder; dorsal horn neurons receive both inputs."
 },
